According to a new report from Intel Market Research, the global Digital Product Engineering Service market was valued at USD 2,239 million in 2024 and is projected to reach USD 3,122 million by 2032, growing at a CAGR of 5.5% during the forecast period (2025–2032). This growth is propelled by accelerating digital transformation initiatives across industries, rising adoption of cloud-native architectures, and increasing demand for AI-powered product development solutions.
What are Digital Product Engineering Services?
Digital Product Engineering Services encompass the comprehensive lifecycle management of technology-driven solutions, integrating cutting-edge tools like artificial intelligence, cloud computing, and IoT. These services enable businesses to design, develop, test, and maintain digital products with enhanced efficiency and superior user experience. The approach combines agile methodologies with DevOps practices to accelerate product development while maintaining rigorous quality standards across diverse industries including healthcare, fintech, and manufacturing.
These services are typically delivered through specialized engineering teams that leverage modern frameworks like microservices architecture, containerization, and continuous integration/continuous deployment (CI/CD) pipelines. The market has evolved from traditional IT services to become a strategic partner for organizations seeking to innovate and maintain competitive advantage in rapidly evolving digital landscapes.
